* ADS7953 internal multiplexer: one channel (Ch0..Ch15 pin -> MXO), behavioral
*
* Pins : s   = channel input pin (Chx)
*        d   = multiplexer output (MXO)
*        c   = analog enable, 0 V = off, 1 V = on (generated by the netlist from the SPI frame schedule)
*
* Global .param values (set by build_model.py from config.json):
*   ads_ron, ads_roff, ads_cs_off, ads_c_ft, ads_qinj, ads_qinj_src_frac, ads_il0, ads_il1, ads_il2 (pin leakage at 0 / 1.25 / 2.5 V)
*
* Datasheet SLAS605C gives the 15 pF input capacitance (modelled at the S/H, not here) and the input leakage vs temperature
* (Figure 43, evaluated at the chosen temperature by build_model.py; a current from every channel pin to ground that depends
* on the pin voltage). Ron, pin / feedthrough capacitance and charge injection are NOT specified by the datasheet: they are
* placeholders (charge injection defaults to 0).
.subckt ADS_CH s d c
Bsw s d I=V(s,d)*(limit(V(c),0,1)/{ads_ron} + (1-limit(V(c),0,1))/{ads_roff})
Cso s 0 {ads_cs_off}
Cft s d {ads_c_ft}
Bqd 0 d I=-{ads_qinj}*(1-{ads_qinj_src_frac})*ddt(limit(V(c),0,1))
Bqs 0 s I=-{ads_qinj}*{ads_qinj_src_frac}*ddt(limit(V(c),0,1))
Blk s 0 I={ads_il0} + ({ads_il1}-{ads_il0})*limit(V(s),0,1.25)/1.25 + ({ads_il2}-{ads_il1})*limit(V(s)-1.25,0,1.25)/1.25
.ends ADS_CH
